<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>God in tongues of fire descending,</l><l>Chosen vessels thus to fill</l><l>With the treasure never ending,</l><l>Ever spent—unfailing still.</l><l>God’s own hand the vessel filling</l><l>From the glory far above,</l><l>Longing hearts forever stilling</l><l>With the riches of His love.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Thus though worn, and tried, and tempted,</l><l>Glorious calling, saint, is thine;</l><l>Let the Lord but find thee emptied,</l><l>Living branch in Christ the Vine!</l><l>Vessels of the world’s despising,</l><l>Vessels weak and poor and base,</l><l>Bearing wealth God’s heart is prizing,</l><l>Glory from Christ’s blessed face.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Oh to be but emptier, lowlier,</l><l>Mean, unnoticed—and unknown,</l><l>And to God a vessel holier,</l><l>Filled with Christ and Christ alone!</l><l>Naught of earth to cloud the glory,</l><l>Naught of self the light to dim,</l><l>Telling forth His wondrous story,</l><l>Emptied to be filled with Him.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
